<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: CZECH FUND SP CESKY 9MONTH GROSS CZK 1.1BLN.</title>
<headline>CZECH FUND SP CESKY 9MONTH GROSS CZK 1.1BLN.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary results for nine</p>
<p>months ending September 30, 1996: (in millions of crowns)</p>
<p> Gross profit	   1,072.342     vs     428.101</p>
<p> Total assets	  11,862.588     vs	   n/a</p>
<p> Value of portfolio  11,278.155     vs	   n/a</p>
<p> Basic capital	  7,735.456     vs   7,735.456</p>
<p>Net asset value</p>
<p> per share (CZK)	  613.410     vs	   n/a</p>
<p>Note. Full name of the investment fund is Sporitelni</p>
<p>Privatizacni - Cesky Investicni Fond a.s. . The fund</p>
<p>is managed by Sporitelni investicni Spolecnost a.s., an</p>
<p>investment arm of savings bank Ceska Sporitelna a.s. .</p>
<p>SP Cesky is listed on the main market of the Prague Stock</p>
<p>Exchange.</p>
<p>Ceska Sporitelna held 26 percent of the fund's shares at</p>
<p>the end of October, and Midland Bank plc held 30</p>
<p>percent.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 42-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
